# Workflow scripts are read verbatim by the Workflow tool, which rejects the
# CR in a CRLF line ending as a control character. Keep them LF on every
# platform so a Windows checkout can still launch them.
.claude/workflows/*.js text eol=lf

# Ledger files every PR is required to prepend to (AGENTS.md 7.1 / 7.2 / 7.2b).
# Two PRs authored in parallel always collide at line 1 on these, on paperwork
# rather than on code -- see #344 "the structural problem".
#
# `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides instead of raising a conflict. That is exactly
# the right outcome here: two independent log entries are additive, and losing
# one silently would be worse than a conflict. It is a transitional safety net,
# not the fix -- #344 WS2 moves new entries to per-PR fragments under
# .changes/unreleased/ and knowledge/problems/, after which these files become
# generated and stop being written by hand at all.
#
# Union merging is only safe for append/prepend-only logs. Never add it to a
# file where two edits could interleave into something meaningless.
CHANGELOG.md            merge=union
PROBLEM_LOG.md          merge=union
knowledge/task-log/INDEX.md merge=union
